OVERVIEW: Perform image segmentation using AI models

Segment anatomical structures or lesions using trained models.
Outputs segmentation masks in various formats.

Example:
  dicom-ai segment ct.dcm --model organ-seg.mlmodel --output seg.dcm --format
dicom-seg

USAGE: dicom-ai segment [<options>] <input> --model <model>

ARGUMENTS:
  <input>                 Path to the DICOM file or directory

OPTIONS:
  -m, --model <model>     CoreML model file path (.mlmodel or .mlmodelc)
  -o, --output <output>   Output file path (prints to stdout if omitted)
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: json, text, csv, dicom-sr, dicom-seg
                          (values: json, text, csv, dicom-sr, dicom-seg;
                          default: json)
  --confidence <confidence>
                          Minimum confidence threshold (0.0-1.0) (default: 0.5)
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output for debugging
  --frame <frame>         Frame index for multi-frame images (default: 0)
                          (default: 0)
  --profile               Enable performance profiling
  --profile-output <profile-output>
                          Output performance metrics to file
  --algorithm-version <algorithm-version>
                          Algorithm Version (111003, DCM) written in the
                          dicom-sr output (PS3.16 TID 4019 row 2, M). Default:
                          the model's CoreML version metadata, else "unknown"
        Algorithm Name (111001, DCM) is the model file name.
  --labels <labels>       Segmentation labels file (JSON with class names)
  --segment-category <segment-category>
                          Segmented Property Category (PS3.16 CID 7150) written
                          for every segment of a dicom-seg output: a keyword or
                          SCHEME:VALUE[:MEANING]. Default: tissue (85756007,
                          SCT, "Tissue") (default: tissue)
        Keywords: tissue, anatomical-structure, physical-object,
        abnormal-structure, function, spatial-concept, body-substance, substance
  --segment-type <segment-type>
                          Segmented Property Type (PS3.16 CID 7151) written for
                          every segment of a dicom-seg output: a keyword or
                          SCHEME:VALUE[:MEANING]. Default: tissue (85756007,
                          SCT, "Tissue") (default: tissue)
        Keywords: tissue, soft-tissue, organ, bone, blood-vessel, muscle, fat,
        lesion, mass, nodule, neoplasm, cyst, heart, brain, liver, kidney,
        spleen, pancreas, lung, prostate, background
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

